    "summary": "The current graph captures the basic scenario of draining a sealed MP odorizer that then ruptured and exploded, but it compresses the core causal chain too much. The most important missing step is the explicitly reported unexpected chemical reaction between the draining/disturbance activity and the vessel rupture. There is also a low-severity schema issue because the hazard consequence evidence is paraphrased rather than quoted verbatim.",
